UID:10020692-1779030000-1779037200@livemusicasheville.com
SUMMARY:Pan Harmonia presents: JOY
DESCRIPTION:WELCOME to Community Chamber Music! \nDonation-based · Pay-as-You-Can concerts \nPan Harmonia\, Asheville’s award winning chamber music company presents JOY for flute\, bassoon\, harp with Kate Steinbeck\, Rosalind Buda\, Jessica Schaeffer Sunday Friday\, May 15th at 7 pm at Black Mountain Presbyterian Church\, Sunday May 17th at 3 pm at First Presbyterian Church of Asheville. John Marson’s delicious Suite of Spring Blooms and Strawberries and Cream in delicate interplay with Adrienne Albert’s inventive Doppler Effect and WNC premiere of composer Frederick Glesser’s Variations on a Theme by Catharina Pratten.\nThese and more favorites of the performers will bring a smile to the face and joy to the heart!\nPan Harmonia offers pay-as-you-can\, donation-based performances; no one is turned away for lack of funds. “Music is for everyone!\,” says Steinbeck. Those that can\, help by donating funds for the musicians and Pan Harmonia operations.\nReserve in advance\nFor more information visit: https://panharmonia.org/events/\nJOYFriday\, May 15th\, 7 pm · Black Mountain Presbyterian ChurchSunday\, May 17th\, 3 pm · First Presbyterian Church of Asheville
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/pan-harmonia-presents-lets-go-retro-2/
LOCATION:First Presbyterian Church of Asheville
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
END:VEVENT
